{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>Or in the warp or in the woof.</b> They are known. And it is possible that the form of שתי is from the paradigm of וחשופי שת, which is a root letter, and the witness is כי השתות יהרסון." "And the meaning of <b>ערב</b> is that it is interwoven (מתערב) with the warp." "<b>Or in the skin.</b> As it is." "<b>In any article of skin.</b> Such as a sieve and a wineskin."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The verse וחשופי שת (Isa. 47:2) and the phrase כי השתות יהרסון (Ps. 11:3) are quoted in Hebrew; the grammatical argument about paradigm and root letter is rendered as Ibn Ezra gives it, compressed and technical."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:57.266039525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}